      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 142,
      "outputTokens": 1130,
      "costUsd": 0.010241,
      "pronunciationText": "Now add the runs up as we go, like the scoreboard does. After one over, the total is S one, just the first term, two. S two adds the first two terms: two plus four is six. Then the scoreboard shows twelve, twenty and thirty. In general, S sub n is the sum of the first n terms. It's called the nth partial sum, a running total. Notice that the totals, two, six, twelve, twenty, thirty, make a new sequence of their own. And each total is the one before it, plus one more over. So S five minus S four leaves just the fifth over's runs: thirty minus twenty is ten."
    },
