      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 119,
      "outputTokens": 817,
      "costUsd": 0.0074125,
      "pronunciationText": "What if the sequence is infinite, like a game whose overs never end? Then the sum of all its terms, a sub one plus a sub two plus a sub three, and so on, is called a series. The partial sums are the steps on the way. For two, plus four, plus six, and so on, the scoreboard just keeps climbing, so this series has no total. Some series do settle on a number, and we'll see which ones in a later video. So, S sub n means the first n terms. A series means all of them."
    },
