      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 134,
      "outputTokens": 1089,
      "costUsd": 0.009868,
      "pronunciationText": "Writing long sums out is slow, so we use sigma notation. Take the first team's runs again: one, three, five, seven. This big symbol is the Greek capital letter sigma, and it means add. Underneath, k equals one tells you where to start. On top, four tells you where to stop. And two k minus one, on the right, is the rule for each term. Each value of k makes one term. Put in k equals one, two, three and four, to get one, three, five and seven. Add them up, and the sum is sixteen, Team A's score after four overs."
    },
