      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 139,
      "outputTokens": 960,
      "costUsd": 0.0087095,
      "pronunciationText": "The start doesn't have to be one. Here's the sum from k equals three to seven, of k squared. The first term uses k equals three, so it's nine. Then come sixteen, twenty-five, thirty-six and forty-nine. That's five terms, not seven, because seven minus three is four, plus one for the first term. The total is one hundred and thirty-five. In general, the sum from k equals i to j, of a sub k, adds every term from a sub i up to a sub j. And k is just ay counter. Use m instead, and the sum is exactly the same."
    },
