      "inputTokens": 132,
      "outputTokens": 1061,
      "costUsd": 0.009615,
      "pronunciationText": "Now write a sum from words. Write the sum of the first ten odd numbers in sigma notation. First, find a rule for the odd numbers. One, three, five, seven: each one is one less than an even number, so the kth odd number is two k minus one. Check: k equals one gives one. Next, the start and the stop. The first ten odd numbers means k goes from one to ten. So it's the sum, from k equals one to ten, of two k minus one. The last term is two times ten, minus one, which is nineteen. And all ten add to one hundred."
    },
