      "pronunciationText": "So a sequence is an ordered list, a sub n is the term in position n, S sub n adds up the first n terms, and sigma writes a sum in one line. Now look at a stack of chairs. One chair is eighty centimetres tall. Two stacked are eighty-six, and three are ninety-two. Each chair adds six. What happens when every step is the same?"
